# BUGS

What xhci(3)'s BUGS say of devices holds here: hubs and HID's boot keyboards and mice only, the first configuration, one transaction translator for a multi-TT hub, and a device's memory kept by the driver when it leaves.
A full- or low-speed device on a root port that isn't a ChipIdea controller's is left to a companion controller, and no companion controller is driven.
Every interrupt endpoint is polled every frame; a high-speed endpoint asking for more than one transaction a microframe gets one.
Only the K1's controllers' host mode is driven: neither their OTG nor their device mode.
